The worker is a Python process that:

Connects to Temporal — polls agent-task-queue for work

Registers activities it can execute:

agent_validatePrompt — asks LLM if user input makes sense for the current goal
agent_toolPlanner — asks LLM what tool to call next and with what args
get_wf_env_vars — reads env vars like SHOW_CONFIRM
mcp_tool_activity — executes a tool via MCP (this is where mobile-mcp/ADB gets called)
mcp_list_tools — discovers what tools an MCP server exposes
Registers the AgentGoalWorkflow — the workflow definition that orchestrates the loop:

Wait for user message → validate → ask LLM what to do → ask user to confirm → execute tool → repeat
Manages MCP connections via MCPClientManager — starts/stops npx @anthropic/mobile-mcp as a subprocess

The synergy would be: your agent calls SlotBot's state detection as a tool, gets back a structured game state ("state": "wild_selection"), and then the LLM decides what to do with that information.
two fundamentally different approaches:

SlotBot	Your Agent
How it works	Deterministic state machine	LLM-driven decisions
Game knowledge	YAML config + OpenCV image templates	Natural language description + screenshots
Language	Java/Kotlin	Python
Platform	Selenium/browser only	Mobile + Web
Handles unexpected states	No — fixed state transitions	Yes — LLM adapts
What it produces	Automated execution	QA report with observations